  "goodToKnow": "Die Stromversorgung is the electricity supply. Germany's grid is among the most reliable in the world, with very few minutes of outage a year. Germany shut down its last nuclear power plants in April 2023, and renewables now supply more than half of its electricity. Der Strom means electricity and also a big river: gegen den Strom schwimmen (to swim against the tide). Der Stromausfall is a power cut. It has no plural."
